  "term": "matching patients",
  "definition": "Matching patients refers to the process of determining whether a patient fits a particular clinical trial by comparing the person’s record with the trial’s eligibility information. In the source packet, this is done with explainable AI using features such as cancer type, performance status, genetic mutation, and measurable disease, and produces a match score with supporting evidence.",
